			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Migrate CocoonMain to Effect-TS architecture and integrate ModuleInterceptor\n\nCompletes the architectural transition of the Cocoon extension host to a purely declarative Effect-TS runtime by refactoring the main entry point and integrating critical security services.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n*   **CocoonMain Refactor:** Replaced legacy imperative initialization in `CocoonMain.ts` with the `EffectServices.composeAppLayer()`. The bootstrap now runs via `NodeRuntime.runMain` and utilizes the centralized `BootstrapTag` for startup orchestration.\n\n*   **ModuleInterceptor Service:** Implemented a new Effect-TS service (`Source/Effect/ModuleInterceptor.ts`) for handling module interception and security sandboxing. It supports security policies (SANDBOXED, TRUSTED, BLOCKED), validates module access, and tracks interception statistics. Integrated as `stage4_ModuleInterceptor` in the `Bootstrap` sequence, ensuring the module system is secured before the RPC server starts.\n\n*   **EchoActionClient:** Introduced `CocoonEchoClient` to manage bidirectional gRPC communication with Mountain. Handles host registration, heartbeat loops, and action dispatching (RPC, Event, State) within the `Cocoon` process.\n\n*   **ServiceMapping Cleanup:** Reorganized `ServiceMapping.ts` to distinct `OldStyleServices` (legacy) and `EffectServices` (modern) namespaces, clarifying the dependency graph and layer composition for the new architecture.\n\n*   **Type & State Fixes:** Corrected `Ref` state mutations in `MountainClient` and `RPCServer` (using `Ref.set`), and decoupled `Window/Types.ts` from direct `vscode` type imports to use strict string literals.",
			"SHA": "8616ea1538dd3b30e01ae8573461d262bbbab7dd"
		},
